    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. You mentioned the timbre as \"ethereal\" because of that sparse distribution. In some orchestral settings, you also get these subtle, almost \"ghostly\" resonance peaks that don't seem to align perfectly with the main series. How do those non-harmonic components or \"ghost notes\" play into the overall texture?",
